METHODE - GET simple valide
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - POST valide avec Content-Length
POST /submit HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 13


======
METHODE - DELETE valide
DELETE /file.txt HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - PUT non supportee -> 405
PUT /file.txt HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - HEAD non supportee -> 405
HEAD / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - CONNECT non supportee -> 405
CONNECT / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - OPTIONS non supportee -> 405
OPTIONS / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - TRACE non supportee -> 405
TRACE / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - PATCH non supportee -> 405
PATCH / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - inconnue FOOBAR -> 400
FOOBAR / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - vide (espace en premiere position) -> 400
 / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
METHODE - minuscule 'get' non reconnue -> 400 (case-sensitive)
get / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
REQUEST LINE - version HTTP/1.1 refusee -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.1
Host: example.com


======
REQUEST LINE - version HTTP/2.0 refusee -> 400
GET / HTTP/2.0
Host: example.com


======
REQUEST LINE - version minuscule 'http/1.0' refusee -> 400
GET / http/1.0
Host: example.com


======
REQUEST LINE - pas de separateur espace du tout -> 400
GET/HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
REQUEST LINE - un seul espace (version manquante) -> 400
GET /
Host: example.com


======
REQUEST LINE - espaces multiples entre elements -> 400 (target devient vide ou decale)
GET  / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
REQUEST LINE - caracteres en trop apres la version -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0X
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - vide -> 400
GET  HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - relatif sans '/' initial -> 400
GET relative/path HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - absolu avec http:// -> OK
GET http://example.com/path HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - avec query string -> OK
GET /search?q=test&page=2 HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - avec caractere de controle (0x01) -> 400
GET /bad HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - avec DEL (0x7F) -> 400
GET /bad HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - exactement 8192 caracteres -> OK (limite incluse)
GET  HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - 8193 caracteres -> 414 (URI Too Long)
GET  HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
TARGET - racine '/' seule -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
STRUCTURE - header totalement vide -> 400 (Header empty)

======
STRUCTURE - juste la request line, pas de ligne vide finale -> 400 (Empty line in Header)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
======
STRUCTURE - request line seule + ligne vide -> OK (aucun header)
GET / HTTP/1.0


======
STRUCTURE - ligne d'en-tete sans deux-points -> 400 (No colon found)
GET / HTTP/1.0
InvalidHeaderLine


======
STRUCTURE - plusieurs headers valides -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
User-Agent: test-client/1.0
Accept: */*


======
STRUCTURE - nom de header vide (ligne commence par ':') -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
: value


======
STRUCTURE - valeur de header vide mais deux-points present -> OK (valeur vide autorisee sauf headers connus)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
X-Custom:


======
STRUCTURE - espaces autour de la valeur trimmes -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
X-Custom:    hello world   


======
HEADER NAME - avec espace -> 400 (non tchar)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Invalid Name: value


======
HEADER NAME - avec caracteres speciaux autorises (tchar) -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
X-Custom!#$%&'*+-.^_`|~: value


======
HEADER NAME - avec deux-points dans le nom (invalide car ':' n'est pas un tchar) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
X:Y: value


======
HEADER VALUE - caractere de controle NUL (0x00) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
X-Test: bad␀value


======
HEADER VALUE - caractere de controle (0x01) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
X-Test: badvalue


======
HEADER VALUE - DEL (0x7F) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
X-Test: badvalue


======
HEADER VALUE - tabulation (0x09) autorisee -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
X-Test: bad	value


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - valeur numerique valide -> OK
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 42


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - zero -> OK
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 0


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - non numerique -> 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: abc


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - vide -> 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - avec signe negatif -> 400 (le '-' n'est pas un digit)
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: -5


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - avec espace au milieu -> 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 4 2


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - duplique avec la MEME valeur -> OK (autorise)
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 10
Content-Length: 10


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - duplique avec des valeurs DIFFERENTES -> 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 10
Content-Length: 20


======
CONTENT-LENGTH - triple avec une valeur differente au milieu -> 400
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Length: 10
Content-Length: 20
Content-Length: 10


======
TRANSFER-ENCODING - present (chunked) -> 501 (non implemente)
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Transfer-Encoding: chunked


======
TRANSFER-ENCODING - casse differente (TRANSFER-ENCODING) -> 501 quand meme
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
TRANSFER-ENCODING: chunked


======
TRANSFER-ENCODING - valeur vide -> 501 quand meme (verifiee avant la valeur)
POST / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Transfer-Encoding:


======
CONNECTION - close -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: close


======
CONNECTION - keep-alive -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: keep-alive


======
CONNECTION - deux valeurs separees par une virgule -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: close, keep-alive


======
CONNECTION - valeur vide -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection:


======
CONNECTION - virgule finale (valeur vide apres) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: close,


======
CONNECTION - double virgule (segment vide au milieu) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: close,,keep-alive


======
CONNECTION - espace au milieu d'une valeur (pas une virgule) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: keep alive


======
CONNECTION - espaces autour de la virgule tolerees -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: close ,  keep-alive


======
CONNECTION - dupliquee (aucune verif de doublon actuellement) -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Connection: close
Connection: keep-alive


======
HOST - hostname simple -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com


======
HOST - hostname avec sous-domaine -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: www.example.com


======
HOST - hostname avec tiret -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: my-server.example.com


======
HOST - hostname avec port -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com:8080


======
HOST - hostname commencant par un tiret -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: -example.com


======
HOST - hostname avec point en debut -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: .example.com


======
HOST - hostname avec point en fin -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com.


======
HOST - hostname avec double point '..' -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example..com


======
HOST - hostname avec caractere invalide (espace) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: exa mple.com


======
HOST - hostname avec port invalide (>65535) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com:99999


======
HOST - hostname avec port non numerique -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com:abcd


======
HOST - valeur vide -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host:


======
HOST - absent de la requete -> pas d'erreur (Host non obligatoire ici)
GET / HTTP/1.0
User-Agent: test


======
HOST - duplique (meme valeur) -> 400 (duplication interdite, contrairement a Content-Length)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Host: example.com


======
HOST - duplique (valeurs differentes) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Host: other.com


======
HOST - purement numerique sans point, ex '12345' -> 400 (classe comme IPv4 potentiel puis rejete)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 12345


======
HOST IPv4 - valide -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 192.168.1.1


======
HOST IPv4 - avec port valide -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 127.0.0.1:8080


======
HOST IPv4 - 0.0.0.0 -> OK (seul 255.255.255.255 est reserve)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 0.0.0.0


======
HOST IPv4 - octet > 255 -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 300.1.1.1


======
HOST IPv4 - reserve 255.255.255.255 -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 255.255.255.255


======
HOST IPv4 - trop peu de groupes (3 au lieu de 4) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 192.168.1


======
HOST IPv4 - trop de groupes (5) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 1.2.3.4.5


======
HOST IPv4 - groupe avec 4 chiffres -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 1922.1.1.1


======
HOST IPv4 - groupe vide (double point) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 192..1.1


======
HOST IPv4 - port invalide (>65535) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: 192.168.1.1:70000


======
HOST IPv6 - complet (8 groupes) valide -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001:0db8:0000:0000:0000:0000:0000:0001]


======
HOST IPv6 - abrege avec '::' valide (loopback) -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [::1]


======
HOST IPv6 - abrege avec '::' au milieu -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001:db8::1]


======
HOST IPv6 - avec port valide -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [::1]:8080


======
HOST IPv6 - deux '::' (invalide, ambigu) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001::db8::1]


======
HOST IPv6 - triple deux-points ':::' -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001:::1]


======
HOST IPv6 - pas assez de groupes sans '::' -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001:db8:1:1:1:1:1]


======
HOST IPv6 - trop de groupes -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001:db8:1:1:1:1:1:1:1]


======
HOST IPv6 - caractere hexadecimal invalide 'g' -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [2001:db8::g]


======
HOST IPv6 - groupe trop long (5 chars) -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [20011:db8::1]


======
HOST IPv6 - sans crochets -> 400 (traite comme IPv4 potentiel puis rejete)
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: ::1


======
HOST IPv6 - crochet fermant manquant -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: [::1


======
CONTENT-TYPE - simple valide -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Type: text/html


======
CONTENT-TYPE - avec parametre charset -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Type: text/html; charset=utf-8


======
CONTENT-TYPE - avec parametre sans espace apres ';' -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Type: text/html;charset=utf-8


======
CONTENT-TYPE - plusieurs parametres -> OK
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=abc123; charset=utf-8


======
CONTENT-TYPE - vide -> 400
GET / HTTP/1.0
Host: example.com
Content-Type:


======
CONTENT-TYPE - sans '/' -> 400
